Subject: [PATCH 10/10] JS API: declare the two CSL effects fields; update the
 integration-test literals

`Effects` gained `claimed_spend_authorizations` (index 9) and
`claimed_output_coverage` (index 10) in the first experiment commit, and
the wasm serializes them as two further arrays. The TypeScript type in
`onchain-runtime-wasm/onchain-runtime-v5.d.ts` now declares them
(`Fr[]`, `CoinCommitment[]`), and the seven `Effects` literals in
`integration-tests/` carry them, so the three `no-proving` tests that
compared whole `Effects` objects (`QueryContext` x2, `functions`) match
again. No change to the Rust code.

The three `proving` integration tests that fail (`Transient` x2,
`TransactionBig`) are a different matter: they prove zswap inputs through
the proof server, which still interprets the shipped zswap IR for
`midnight/zswap/spend` and rejects the CSL preimage ("Expected 77 inputs,
received 87"). Proving CSL spends through the proof server is not
supported on this branch; see the experiment record.

